   "t": 1791259387.692857,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "My search stopped cleanly on the pre-declared rule. Final specification: **feature 0 (short), feature 12 (short)**, equal-weight combination, in-sample Sharpe = 1.2212.\n\nNow I'll form my out-of-sample belief. Key considerations:\n- This is a 2-feature spec found after only 2 content moves (init + 1 extend), with a disciplined pre-registered stop \u2014 this is relatively light search, so overfitting risk is lower than if I'd run many more trials.\n- Still, in-sample Sharpe typically overstates out-of-sample performance due to selection effects (I did pick the best single feature, then the best extension among 78 candidates).\n- Costs are already netted in (5bps turnover, 50bps borrow, 1-day lag), so the in-sample number is a reasonably \"real\" backtest rather than a gross fantasy number.\n- A reasonable haircut for a 2-feature spec selected from a reasonably sized candidate pool (40 features) with only two selection steps: shrink toward something like 50-65% of in-sample, with substantial uncertainty."
  },
