    "note": "In-sample Sharpe 1.2212 from spec [feature 0 short, feature 12 short], equal-weight, found via init (best single feature) + one extend_best (best pairwise addition among 78 candidates), net of costs. Search was short (2 content moves) and stopped on a pre-declared trigger rather than continued probing, which limits overfitting from extensive trial-and-error. Still, selecting the best of 40 features then best of 78 pairwise extensions induces some upward bias in the in-sample figure. I haircut substantially (~45-55% retained) to account for selection effects and regime/feature instability out of sample, with wide uncertainty given only two features and no out-of-sample validation set available to me."
