   "text": "Submitted. Summary of the session:\n\n**Process:**\n1. Declared three stopping rules upfront: stop if best-so-far Sharpe exceeds 1.2, stop after 2 failures, or stop if the last gain is \u22640.02.\n2. `init` \u2014 anchored on the single best feature (feature 0, short sign), Sharpe 1.095.\n3. `extend_best` \u2014 added the best complementary feature (feature 12, short sign), Sharpe rose to 1.2212.\n4. This crossed my pre-declared `best_so_far_above` bar of 1.2, which licensed (and required, by my own discipline) a stop rather than further probing \u2014 honoring the rule chosen *before* seeing any results, rather than chasing more gains after the fact.\n\n**Final specification:** Equal-weight short position in feature 0 and feature 12.\n- In-sample annualized Sharpe (net of costs): **1.2212**\n- Predicted out-of-sample Sharpe: **mean 0.65, sd 0.45**\n\nThe haircut from 1.22 to 0.65 reflects standard selection-effect shrinkage (best-of-40 then best-of-78 extension), even though the search itself was short and stopped on a rule fixed in advance rather than optimized post-hoc."
